## struct.rs.vm
## Generates a Rust struct for an IDL struct.
##
## Mapping:
##   IDL struct -> #[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq)] pub struct.
##
## COPY SEMANTICS — unlike the C# mapping (a reference-type `sealed class`
## that requires an explicit deep-copy constructor at every UoP boundary; see
## docs/csharp-binding-guide.md §6.2), a Rust struct is a plain value type.
## Ownership and the borrow checker rule out the aliasing bug that guide
## warns about; `Clone` is derived so an explicit, visible `.clone()` is all
## that is ever needed to obtain an independent copy.
##
## Not derived: Default. It would be a nice zero-argument-constructor
## equivalent, but any struct with a field typed as a generated union
## (union.rs.vm) can never derive it -- Rust's #[default] attribute is only
## legal on a unit enum variant, and a union's cases always carry a payload
## (see union.rs.vm) -- so it is left off uniformly rather than only on the
## structs that happen to embed one. Construct instances with struct-literal
## syntax instead.
##
## Context:
##   $struct — StructNode
##   $types  — TypeResolver
##
## Generated by Entity Reactor IDL Generator.
#![allow(non_snake_case, non_camel_case_types)]
##
/// Rust struct for IDL struct `${struct.name}`.
#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq)]
pub struct $types.safeName($struct.name) {
#foreach($member in $struct.members)
    /// IDL member `${member.name}`.
    pub $types.safeName($member.name): #rustType($member.type),
#end
}
